{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts alpinejs","lang":"sh"},{"type":"code","value":"import Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { charts } from '@tanstack/charts/alpine'\n\nAlpine.plugin(charts)\nAlpine.start()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<div x-data=\"{ chartOptions }\" x-chart=\"chartOptions\"></div>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directive element owns its contents. Alpine effects forward option changes\nto the shared host and directive cleanup destroys the runtime."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"charts"},{"type":"text","value":" registers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-chart"},{"type":"text","value":". The directive evaluates its expression inside an\nAlpine effect, creates one shared adapter controller, and forwards each\ncomplete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" value. Cleanup destroys the controller, removes the\nsurface, and restores the element's prior inline layout and host class."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-only-contract","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser-only contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directive requires Alpine and normal DOM APIs. It does not prerender a\nserver shell or provide a hydration path. Start it in the browser after\nregistering "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alpine.plugin(charts)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"presentation-and-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation and rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directive element itself becomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":"; normal HTML class and\nstyle attributes own its presentation. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" chart option applies\nto the rendered chart surface. The directive starts with SVG and can compose\nmarks that use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" to replace SVG\nserialization without replacing the shared host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"charts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AlpineChartTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const chartOptions = {\n  definition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue',\n  renderTooltipBody({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) {\n    const body = document.createElement('div')\n    body.append(defaultBody)\n    body.append(`Focused rows: ${points.length}`)\n    if (pinned) {\n      const close = document.createElement('button')\n      close.textContent = 'Close'\n      close.addEventListener('click', dismiss)\n      body.append(close)\n    }\n    return body\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state,\npinning, and dismissal. Alpine owns the returned DOM content."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"lifecycle","text":"Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"browser-only-contract","text":"Browser-only contract","level":2},{"id":"presentation-and-rendering","text":"Presentation and rendering","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts alpinejs\n```\n\n```ts\nimport Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { charts } from '@tanstack/charts/alpine'\n\nAlpine.plugin(charts)\nAlpine.start()\n```\n\n```html\n<div x-data=\"{ chartOptions }\" x-chart=\"chartOptions\"></div>\n```\n\nThe directive element owns its contents. Alpine effects forward option changes\nto the shared host and directive cleanup destroys the runtime.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n`charts` registers `x-chart`. The directive evaluates its expression inside an\nAlpine effect, creates one shared adapter controller, and forwards each\ncomplete `ChartOptions` value. Cleanup destroys the controller, removes the\nsurface, and restores the element's prior inline layout and host class.\n\n## Browser-only contract\n\nThe directive requires Alpine and normal DOM APIs. It does not prerender a\nserver shell or provide a hydration path. Start it in the browser after\nregistering `Alpine.plugin(charts)`.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\nThe directive element itself becomes `.ts-chart-host`; normal HTML class and\nstyle attributes own its presentation. The `className` chart option applies\nto the rendered chart surface. The directive starts with SVG and can compose\nmarks that use `canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG\nserialization without replacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `charts`, `ChartOptions`, `ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`,\n`AlpineChartTooltipBody`, `ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n```ts\nconst chartOptions = {\n  definition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue',\n  renderTooltipBody({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) {\n    const body = document.createElement('div')\n    body.append(defaultBody)\n    body.append(`Focused rows: ${points.length}`)\n    if (pinned) {\n      const close = document.createElement('button')\n      close.textContent = 'Close'\n      close.addEventListener('click', dismiss)\n      body.append(close)\n    }\n    return body\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state,\npinning, and dismissal. Alpine owns the returned DOM content.\n\nSee the [`x-chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Alpine Adapter\ndescription: Mount TanStack Charts with an Alpine directive.\n---\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts alpinejs\n```\n\n```ts\nimport Alpine from 'alpinejs'\nimport { charts } from '@tanstack/charts/alpine'\n\nAlpine.plugin(charts)\nAlpine.start()\n```\n\n```html\n<div x-data=\"{ chartOptions }\" x-chart=\"chartOptions\"></div>\n```\n\nThe directive element owns its contents. Alpine effects forward option changes\nto the shared host and directive cleanup destroys the runtime.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n`charts` registers `x-chart`. The directive evaluates its expression inside an\nAlpine effect, creates one shared adapter controller, and forwards each\ncomplete `ChartOptions` value. Cleanup destroys the controller, removes the\nsurface, and restores the element's prior inline layout and host class.\n\n## Browser-only contract\n\nThe directive requires Alpine and normal DOM APIs. It does not prerender a\nserver shell or provide a hydration path. Start it in the browser after\nregistering `Alpine.plugin(charts)`.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\nThe directive element itself becomes `.ts-chart-host`; normal HTML class and\nstyle attributes own its presentation. The `className` chart option applies\nto the rendered chart surface. The directive starts with SVG and can compose\nmarks that use `canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG\nserialization without replacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `charts`, `ChartOptions`, `ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`,\n`AlpineChartTooltipBody`, `ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n```ts\nconst chartOptions = {\n  definition,\n  ariaLabel: 'Revenue',\n  renderTooltipBody({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) {\n    const body = document.createElement('div')\n    body.append(defaultBody)\n    body.append(`Focused rows: ${points.length}`)\n    if (pinned) {\n      const close = document.createElement('button')\n      close.textContent = 'Close'\n      close.addEventListener('click', dismiss)\n      body.append(close)\n    }\n    return body\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state,\npinning, and dismissal. Alpine owns the returned DOM content.\n\nSee the [`x-chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n"}
